{ Let’s push our e pawn again. }
3. e3 (3. e4 { You seriously need to get better at chess. } { [%csl Ge4][%cal Gf6e4,Gd5e4] } 3... Nxe4 4. Bd3 Nf6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. h3 Bxf3 7. Qxf3 e6 8. O-O Bd6 9. Bxd6 Qxd6) 3... e6 { This looks absolutely ridiculous, since it blocks their bishop. However, it’s one of the most common moves and one of the best moves according to stockfish. Do not overthink this move because of that, and simply form our wedge. } { [%cal Gc8h3] } 4. c3 Bd6 { This is one of the most popular moves, again. We should take their bishop, since it’s too powerful in its current position. } { [%cal Gd6f8,Gd6a3,Gd6h2] } 5. Bxd6 (5. Bg3 { Well... we're going to castle kingside. This would weaken it. We don't want that. }) 5... Qxd6 { Now we move our bishop into that powerful square shown in the first chapter. } { [%csl Gd3,Gf1] } 6. Bd3 c5 { Let’s continue following the golden moves, moving the knight on b1. } 7. Nd2 O-O { Develop the knight to f3 } { [%csl Gg1] } 8. Ngf3 { This is good. } 8... c4 { Just retreat to c2. } 9. Bc2 { [%cal Gd1e2,Ge1g1,Gh1f1] } *


