2... c5 { This time they strike immediately. Let’s defend with our c pawn. } 3. c3 Nc6 { Now they play Nc6. Let’s create the wedge again. } 4. e3 { [%csl Gd4,Gc3,Gb2,Ge3,Gf2] } 4... Qb6 { The play Qb6. Of course, we defend with our queen by moving it to c2. } 5. Qc2 Nf6 { Now play Nf3, simply developing. } 6. Nf3 { This is a good position for us. } { [%cal Gf1e2,Gf1d3,Gb1d2,Ge1g1,Gh1f1] } 6... g6 { Develop the knight to the best square. } { [%csl Gb1] } 7. Nbd2 Bg7 { Where is the best square for our bishop? } { [%csl Gf1] } 8. Be2 O-O { Castle. } 9. O-O { We’re pretty dominant and have ok winning chances. } *


