3... Qb6 { Now they play Qb6, and we respond by protecting our pawn. } 4. Qc2 (4. b3 { This move just downright sucks. }) (4. Qb3 { This also works, but they have c4. } 4... c4 5. Qxb6 axb6 { [%csl Gf1,Gg1,Gb1,Ga1,Gh1][%cal Ga8a3] }) 4... Nf6 { And now we finish the wedge } 5. e3 { [%csl Ge3,Gc3,Gd4,Gb2,Gf2] } 5... Nc6 { Now let’s simply develop our knight to f3 } 6. Nf3 g6 { Develop our knight to d2. } 7. Nbd2 Bg7 { Develop to e2. } { [%cal Gf1e2] } 8. Be2 (8. Ke2? { Not your king, bozo. }) 8... O-O { Let’s get our king to safety too. } 9. O-O (9. O-O-O?! { This castles right into black’s pawn storm. } 9... c4 10. h3 Bf5 11. Qa4 Bd7 12. Qa3 (12. Qc2 Qa5 13. b4 Qb6 14. Ne5 a5 15. b5 Qxb5) 12... Rfc8 13. h4 a5 14. h5 Qd8 15. Nxc4 b5 16. Ng5 dxc4 { and we’re losing. These pawns are a nuisance and are scary for our king. } { [%cal Gb5b1,Ga5a1,Gc4c1,Ga8a1,Gd8a5,Gc8c1] }) *


